# Published models
#
# id  tier  sha256  filename
#
# Nothing is published yet, and until something is, the format is free to move.
#
# Once a line appears here it is permanent. A model id names the statistics a
# payload was coded against, so a link minted under id 3 only decodes correctly
# under id 3 — for as long as that link exists, which is forever. A published
# model is therefore never re-edited and its id is never reassigned; a retrain
# gets a new id and the old file stays distributed.
#
# The model files themselves are release assets, not source: at Max they are
# ~90 MB, which does not belong in a git history. The hashes belong here, in
# the repository, because a link whose model was lost is a dead link and the
# hash is what proves a recovered copy is the right one.
